                <pb facs="0086" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg54"/>

                <head>35. Telegram From the Joint Chiefs of Staff to the
                    Commander in Chief, U.S. Naval Forces, Eastern Atlantic and Mediterranean
                        (Holloway), at
                        London<anchor n="1" xml:id="d35-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-05-14T17:28:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                                1958—5:28 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>JCS 941782. USNMR pass to SACEUR.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>UK governmental position: <list>
                            <label>a.</label>
                            <item>Command of combined forces used in Lebanon operations will be
                                United States.</item>
                            <label>b.</label>
                            <item>For both political and military reasons United States forces
                                should precede UK forces into
                                Lebanon.</item>
                            <label>c.</label>
                            <item>These two points agreeable to State Dept and approved by JCS.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>FYI. British suggest detailed planning
                        should be done in Mediterranean and not in London.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
